{"name":"Firenze","hex":"#bc7256","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Firenze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Florence:\n\nA city and comune, the capital of the Metropolitan City of Florence and the region of Tuscany, Italy.\nA metropolitan city of Tuscany, established in 2015; in full, the Metropolitan City of Florence.","A city and comune, the capital of the Metropolitan City of Florence and the region of Tuscany, Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Firenze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firenze (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Firenze (1884–1902), also recorded as \"Firenzi\", was an American Thoroughbred Hall of Fame racehorse. During her six-year racing career, she won 47 of 82 starts and retired as the second-highest money-earning filly in American history. She was retroactively named the American Champion Three-Year-Old Filly of 1887 and American Champion Older Female Horse for three straight years. She repeatedly defeated the top colts of the day including the future Hall of Famers, Hanover and Kingston. In the 1888 season, she was the only horse to beat Preakness Stakes winner, The Bard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Album_of_celebrated_American_and_English_running_horses_%28Plate_7%29_%286012487558%29.jpg/330px-Album_of_celebrated_American_and_English_running_horses_%28Plate_7%29_%286012487558%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firenze_(horse)"},{"title":"Florence","blocks":[{"text":"Florence is the capital and most populous city of the Italian region of Tuscany, and, as of 2026, with a population of 361,625, the 8th most populous city in the country. It is also the capital of the eponymous metropolitan province, which counts 988,494 inhabitants, while Eurostat estimates that 696,767 people live in the urban area of Florence. The Metropolitan Area of Florence, Prato and Pistoia, constituted in 2000 over an area of roughly 4,800 square kilometres (1,850 sq mi), is home to 1.5 million people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Firenze_-_Piazzale_Michelangelo%2C_Firenze%2C_Italy_-_April_6%2C_2015_02.jpg/330px-Firenze_-_Piazzale_Michelangelo%2C_Firenze%2C_Italy_-_April_6%2C_2015_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florence"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Totila_fa_dstruggere_la_citt%C3%A0_di_Firenze.jpg/500px-Totila_fa_dstruggere_la_citt%C3%A0_di_Firenze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Totila_fa_dstruggere_la_citt%C3%A0_di_Firenze.jpg/500px-Totila_fa_dstruggere_la_citt%C3%A0_di_Firenze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Goth King Totila razes the walls of Florence during the Gothic War: illumination from the Chigi manuscript of Villani's Cronica","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATotila_fa_dstruggere_la_citt%C3%A0_di_Firenze.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Colored_woodcut_town_view_of_Florence.jpg/500px-Colored_woodcut_town_view_of_Florence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Colored_woodcut_town_view_of_Florence.jpg/500px-Colored_woodcut_town_view_of_Florence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of Florence by Hartmann Schedel, published in 1493","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColored_woodcut_town_view_of_Florence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Francesco_Rosselli_%28attribution%29._Pianta_della_Catena%2C_1470.jpg/500px-Francesco_Rosselli_%28attribution%29._Pi